  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe donor's tax rate under the Tax Reform for Acceleration and Inclusion (TRAIN) law is six percent (6%) on the total gifts exceeding Two Hundred Fifty Thousand Pesos (₱250,000).\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThis is governed by Section 99 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which states that the tax for each calendar year shall be six percent (6%) computed on the basis of the total gifts in excess of ₱250,000.\n\n### Interpretation\nUnder Section 99 of the NIRC, any gifts made by a donor that exceed the exemption threshold of ₱250,000 are subject to a donor's tax at a rate of 6%. This means that only the amount of gifts that surpass this threshold will be taxed, while gifts up to this amount are exempt from the donor's tax.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, individuals making gifts should be aware that they can give up to ₱250,000 in total without incurring any donor's tax liability. However, any amount above this threshold will be taxed at 6%, which necessitates careful planning for larger gifts to manage potential tax implications effectively.",
